.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH RANMA-OPEN 1 "" "ranma 0.1.0" "ranma manual"
.SH NAME
ranma\-open \- Open a pane somewhere, e.g. \fBranma open \-\-session ai \-\-workspace empty \-\-cwd ~/projects/x \-\-name x \-\- \*(Aqai; exec zsh\*(Aq\fR. One argument after \fB\-\-\fR is a command line for the shell; several are a command and its arguments
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBranma open\fR [\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-workspace\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-workspace\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-cwd\fR] [\fB\-\-accent\fR] [\fB\-\-beside\fR] [\fB\-\-side\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-background\fR] [\fB\-\-float\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-print\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open a pane somewhere, e.g. \fBranma open \-\-session ai \-\-workspace empty \-\-cwd ~/projects/x \-\-name x \-\- \*(Aqai; exec zsh\*(Aq\fR. One argument after \fB\-\-\fR is a command line for the shell; several are a command and its arguments
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fI<SESSION>\fR
Switch to this session, creating it if there is none
.TP
\fB\-\-workspace\fR \fI<WORKSPACE>\fR
Then to this workspace: a number, next, prev or empty
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name the pane
.TP
\fB\-\-workspace\-name\fR \fI<WORKSPACE_NAME>\fR
Name the workspace it lands in
.TP
\fB\-\-cwd\fR \fI<CWD>\fR
Start in this directory instead of the focused pane\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-accent\fR \fI<ACCENT>\fR
Colour the session it lands in: #rrggbb, 0\-255 or an ANSI name
.TP
\fB\-\-beside\fR \fI<BESIDE>\fR
Open it beside this pane (an id from \fBranma panes\fR), in that pane\*(Aqs session and workspace, on the \-\-side given
.TP
\fB\-\-side\fR \fI<SIDE>\fR
With \-\-beside: left, right, up or down (default right)
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-background\fR
Leave focus, the session and the workspace as they are
.TP
\fB\-\-float\fR \fI<WIDTH>\fR\fI \fR\fI<HEIGHT>\fR
Float it, centred: width and height in percent of the workspace
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-print\fR
Print the new pane\*(Aqs id
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
What to run; the shell when left out
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBranma\fR(1)
